> integration architecture (left) (Supplementary Sections A.7–A.11) uses
> published model outputs (top) to calibrate emulators and project them at high
> resolution. Where available, several studies are meta-analysed. Damages are then
> aggregated across channels and risk aversion is calculated (bottom). Missing
> risk calculations (centre) (Supplementary Section B.11) rely on expert-assessed
> ranges and indicative estimates (top), projected accounting for double-counting
> and covariance and combined under meta-analysis with an estimate based on
> known risks. The same welfare aggregation is then used. Trade spillovers (right)
> (Supplementary Section B.9) are estimated using three macro-econometric
> models, projected at a national level globally and combined by meta-analysis.
> CGE estimates are used to translate export losses (assumed to scale with foreign
> GDP losses) into UK GDP loss, before being combined in the welfare calculation
> (bottom).
