> towards net-zero. The local co-benefits of net-zero action within the
> UK may be about 4.1% of GDP, net of mitigation costs (Supplementary
> Section C.3) and, combined with the avoided climate damages from
> global mitigation action (6.5% of GDP), amount to 10.6% of GDP by the
> end of the century. Equivalently, the costs of inaction, locally and globally, to the UK economy are 10.6% of GDP. The existence of such large
> benefits for a relatively cool and low-vulnerability country suggests
> that the benefits of mitigation across a wide range of countries may
> be much greater than previously supposed.
